# oracle: pair_style meam, single element bcc reference (w15meam_bcc_lib.meam + w15meam_bcc.meam, zbl 0), 2x2x2 bcc cell (16 atoms), 0.05 A sinusoidal displacement, velocities from atom-style variables, fix nve, 50 steps of 0.001 ps
# oracle: shells of the bcc reference at re = 2.73664 A: 8 nearest neighbours at 2.737 A, 6 second neighbours at 3.16 A (screened to zero by the 1NN), 12 third neighbours at 4.47 A (outside rc = 4.0); the 0.05 A displacements keep every pair distance in [2.5, 3.4] A, away from the cutoff window [3.9, 4.0]
# oracle-inputs: w15meam_bcc_lib.meam w15meam_bcc.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-6 abs=1e-9
# oracle-tolerance: rel=1e-6 is needed for press only (the same offset as w12meam_fcc). Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the native press at step 0 is 9249.30804 bar and the engine's is 9249.31015 bar (2.3e-7 relative); pe agrees to better than 1e-9 relative.
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         bcc 3.16
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 183.84
variable        dx atom 0.05*sin(2.3*x+1.1*y+0.4*z)
variable        dy atom 0.05*cos(1.9*y-0.7*x+0.3*z)
variable        dz atom 0.05*sin(1.3*z+0.8*x-0.5*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.4*cos(1.7*y-0.6*z)
variable        vy atom 0.4*sin(1.2*z+0.9*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*cos(2.1*x-0.8*y+0.2)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w15meam_bcc_lib.meam W w15meam_bcc.meam W
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             50
